WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:08.305
One summer a young grasshopper moved into a forest.

2
00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:14.403
"What a beautiful place!" he thought. "I'll live here."

3
00:00:14.404 --> 00:00:18.626
The happy grasshopper did a little dance.

4
00:00:18.627 --> 00:00:24.528
Soon a group of ants marched by, carrying green leaves and grass.

5
00:00:24.529 --> 00:00:30.054
"Hello, new neighbors!" Grasshopper waved.

6
00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:32.637
"Would you like to play with me?"

7
00:00:32.638 --> 00:00:36.276
"We're busy today," the ants said.

8
00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:40.480
"We don't have time to play."

9
00:00:40.481 --> 00:00:43.914
"Come on!" Grasshopper said.

10
00:00:43.915 --> 00:00:49.220
"It's a beautiful day. We'll have so much fun."

11
00:00:49.221 --> 00:00:57.097
"Sorry," the ants said before marching away.

12
00:00:57.098 --> 00:01:01.063
The next day Grasshopper woke up late.

13
00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:04.227
He saw the ants marching by again.

14
00:01:04.228 --> 00:01:10.121
"Hi there, neighbors!" he said.

15
00:01:10.122 --> 00:01:13.905
"Why are you out so early?"

16
00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:17.445
"It's not early," one ant said.

17
00:01:17.446 --> 00:01:20.536
"We're working," another said.

18
00:01:20.537 --> 00:01:25.745
"Why do you need to work so much?" Grasshopper asked.

19
00:01:25.746 --> 00:01:31.298
"We're gathering food for winter," a little ant said.

20
00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:39.513
"Winter?" Grasshopper laughed.

21
00:01:39.514 --> 00:01:43.243
"It's summer!

22
00:01:43.244 --> 00:01:50.733
It's too early to get ready for winter! How foolish!"

23
00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:54.738
"You're foolish!" an ant said.

24
00:01:54.739 --> 00:01:58.681
"Why?" Grasshopper asked.

25
00:01:58.682 --> 00:02:07.227
"You'll see," the ant warned him.

26
00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:14.662
As summer passed, Grasshopper spent each day having fun.

27
00:02:14.663 --> 00:02:19.459
He slept late.

28
00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:25.278
Then he danced and played.

29
00:02:25.279 --> 00:02:31.190
"You work too much," Grasshopper said whenever the ants went by.

30
00:02:31.191 --> 00:02:39.374
"You play too much," the ants said.

31
00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:43.917
Soon fall arrived, and the forest changed colors.

32
00:02:43.918 --> 00:02:48.130
Leaves fell from trees, and the grass turned brown.

33
00:02:48.131 --> 00:02:57.614
Grasshopper still played every day, and the ants were busier than ever.

34
00:02:57.615 --> 00:03:02.170
One morning Grasshopper woke up, feeling cold.

35
00:03:02.171 --> 00:03:06.158
When he opened his eyes, he saw it was snowing.

36
00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:13.266
Snow covered the ground, and all the trees were bare.

37
00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:17.501
"Brr." Grasshopper shivered.

38
00:03:17.502 --> 00:03:25.455
"Winter is here. I should look for food."

39
00:03:25.456 --> 00:03:31.786
Grasshopper searched the snowy forest but couldn't find anything to eat.

40
00:03:31.787 --> 00:03:36.535
The next day Grasshopper still couldn't find any food.

41
00:03:36.536 --> 00:03:39.622
He searched long and hard.

42
00:03:39.623 --> 00:03:48.737
Eventually he found the ants' home.

43
00:03:48.738 --> 00:03:52.463
"Please," Grasshopper begged.

44
00:03:52.464 --> 00:04:00.274
"Where can I find food? I'm so hungry!"

45
00:04:00.275 --> 00:04:04.020
"It's too late," one ant said.

46
00:04:04.021 --> 00:04:09.675
Another nodded. "You won't find any food until spring."

47
00:04:09.676 --> 00:04:19.578
"What will I do?" Grasshopper sobbed.

48
00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:22.985
The little ant looked at the other ants.

49
00:04:22.986 --> 00:04:27.098
"Grasshopper will die without food."

50
00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:31.182
The others sighed.

51
00:04:31.183 --> 00:04:36.859
"Fine," one said. "There is only one thing to do."

52
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:42.837
That winter Grasshopper stayed with the ants.

53
00:04:42.838 --> 00:04:46.815
They shared their food with him.

54
00:04:46.816 --> 00:04:55.393
Grasshopper was thankful for their kindness, and he learned an important lesson.

55
00:04:55.394 --> 00:05:00.444
As soon as spring arrived, Grasshopper darted outside.

56
00:05:00.445 --> 00:05:04.119
"Where are you going?" the little ant asked.

57
00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:07.114
Grasshopper smiled.

58
00:05:07.115 --> 00:05:14.924
"I have work to do. I must gather food for winter!"

